  "id": "Compound::DB01288 - Gene::153",
  "verbalization": "Fenoterol, a selective beta-2 adrenergic receptor agonist, is shown to bind to Adrb3, a receptor that participates in multiple biological processes. These processes include Beta-adrenergic Receptor Activity and Norepinephrine Binding, both of which are participated by Adrb1. Similarly, Fenoterol binds to Adrb3 and Adrb1 is involved in Epinephrine Binding. The integrated evidence suggests that Fenoterol may exert its effects through a mechanism involving Adrb3, which in turn interacts with Adrb1 through shared functional pathways. The observed scores indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Fenoterol and Adrb1, likely mediated through Adrb3. The evidence supports a potential role for Adrb1 in the pharmacological response to Fenoterol, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
